[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?1049h\u001b[22;0;0t\u001b[23;1H\u001b[?1h\u001b=\r\u001b[1;32mFrom issue to merge in the terminal: the git and gh workflow\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[2m1 Sep, 2026 · 5 min read · CLI, git, GitHub, Open source\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\nThe issue-to-merge loop is nine commands in git and gh. The catch: the branch\u001b[m\r\nlinked to an issue does not close it, only a Closes keyword in the PR body does.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\nFiling an issue, branching, opening the pull request and merging it all run in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[36mgit\u001b[0m and \u001b[36mgh\u001b[0m, with no browser tab open. The whole loop is nine commands.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\nI kept this as a \u001b[4;32mpublic gist\u001b[0m\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m(https://gist.github.com/typovrak/8034fe822905c3febbe4c3c9a84f065d)\u001b[0m for two\u001b[m\r\nyears and run it on every repo I touch. This post is that gist, with the flags\u001b[m\r\nthat skip the prompts and t       "]
[0.000, "o", "     "]
[0.000, "o", "   "]
[0.000, "o", " 0"]
[0.000, "o", "\r1"]
[0.000, "o", "00  11"]
[0.000, "o", "215"]
[0.000, "o", " 100 "]
[0.000, "o", " "]
[0.000, "o", "1"]
[0.000, "o", "12"]
[0.000, "o", "15 "]
[0.000, "o", " "]
[0.000, "o", " 0   "]
[0.000, "o", "   0"]
[0.000, "o", "he one line that makes the merge close the issue for\u001b[m\r\nyou.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\nEverything below is \u001b[36mgh\u001b[0m \u001b[4;32m2.96.0\u001b[0m\u001b[2m (https://github.com/cli/cli/releases/tag/v2.96.0)\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\nand \u001b[36mgit\u001b[0m \u001b[4;32m2.54.0\u001b[0m\u001b[2m (https://github.com/git/git/releases/tag/v2.54.0)\u001b[0m, run from\u001b[m\r\ninside a repository you can push to.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1;32mTable of contents\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", ":\u001b[K "]
[0.000, "o", "102"]
[0.000, "o", ".7k "]
[0.000, "o", "     "]
[0.000, "o", "0"]
[0.000, "o", "    "]
[0.000, "o", "        "]
[0.000, "o", " "]
[0.000, "o", "   "]
[0.000, "o", "    "]
[0.000, "o", "    "]
[0.000, "o", "   "]
[0.000, "o", "   "]
[0.000, "o", "0"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.646, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.160, "o", "\r\u001b[K• The whole loop\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.136, "o", "\r\u001b[K• What actually closes the issue?\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.124, "o", "\r\u001b[K• Which merge strategy?\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.136, "o", "\r\u001b[K• Does this work on a repo you cannot push to?\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.143, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.660, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[1;32mThe whole loop\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[2m─── bash ────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.041, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgh issue create                         # file it, note the number (say 32)\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.039, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgh issue develop 32 --checkout          # branch linked to #32, checked out locally\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[K# write the code, then:\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.041, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgit add .\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgit commit -m 'feat(translation): this is an example'\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgit push\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgh pr create --fill --body \"Closes #32\" # open the PR, keyword set\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch    # rebase onto main, close #32, drop the branch\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[Kgit switch main && git pull --prune     # bring the merge home, tidy stale refs\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.041, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[2m─────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.040, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.041, "o", "\r\u001b[KRun \u001b[36mgh auth login\u001b[0m once and every command after that runs as you. \u001b[36mgh\u001b[0m works out\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.099, "o", "\r\u001b[Kwhich repository you mean from the git remote of the current directory, so all\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.118, "o", "\r\u001b[Kof this happens from inside the checkout.\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.154, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.177, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM• The whole loop\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[23;1H\r\u001b[K:\u001b[K"]
[0.212, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.147, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[36mgh issue create\u001b[0m prints the URL of the issue it filed, and the number on the end\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.247, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[0.000, "o", "of that URL is the \u001b[36m32\u001b[0m every later command refers to. To pick up an issue that\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.153, "o", "\r\u001b[Kalready exists instead, list them and read the number off the left column:\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.141, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n:\u001b[K"]
[0.255, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[?1l\u001b>\u001b[?1049l\u001b[23;0;0t"]
